A||||7||Shaun41178||Raced a 89 Supra Turbo
Z||000000||Shaun41178||06-19-99||03:33 AM||||i went out racing last night and happened to run into an 89 supra <br>turbo.  I found out later from a friend of mine who knew the owner of the car <br>and that it was an 89.<br>	Anyway I am driving down the raod and i am out looking for a good street race.  I see an import with a huge wing drive by along with a 4th gen camaro.  I pull a u-turn and head back in the opposite direction.  Both cars <br>caught a red light ahead<p>anyways I am expecting the camaro and supra to go at it and I am <br>right behind the camaro.  Turns out the camaro is a v6 so he dosen't do anything off the line.  While waiting at the light I notice that the supra says turbo on the back and it has a 55 gallon drum for an exhaust tip.  It also had a huge aftermarket wing.  The car did look very nice I must say.<br>	So after leaving the light and the camaro not doing anything I switch lanes and get  in behind the supra who speeds ahead and gets in the other lane.  We are doing about 45 and he is giving a little punch every now and then as I catch up.  We get side by side and i give it a little punch and then we both hit it.   i immediately grabbed about a 1/4 car lenght or so.  His front bumper was at my rear qtr when I had to shut down as I was quickly approaching a car ahead.  There was no car ahead for the Supra so he just flew by.  I kept trying to get another race but to no avail.  So I pulled another u-turn and headed back in the same direction as I was originally going.  Win no. 1??<br>	So I was driving for a while and a red 88-90 TA flys by along with a grand am so I punch it to catch up and lucky me I catch a redlight with the TA.  I was reving it but he did not rev back as I don't think he could hear it over his radio.  So I was unsure if he wanted to race or not.  I was ready <br>just in case though.  He started slow out of the hole and then punched it.  Seeing this i dropped the hammer and the tires were sent a blazing.  Very loud I must say.  I quickly pulled ahead of this guy and by 60 I had about 4-5 car lengths on him.  Not even close so I shut it down.    wanted a race from a role but to no avail.  Definately win no. 2.<br>	<br>Almost had a race with a N/A eagle talon.  I reved at him at a light and he reved back so the light turned green but he wimped out and turned into a gas station on the corner. Talk about loser.<br>	Then the ultimate.  I ran across a Acura NSX.  Not too many here in Toledo.  So I follow him and get along side at about 45 and start punching it real quick to see if I could get him to go.  To no avail though.  So we come to a light which is red and he looks over so I point ahead. He rolls down his <br>window apparently not knowing what I am talking about so i ask him if he wants to race.  He says "no"  so I say ok no prob, take care.  That would have been a nice race even though I would've lost I still would've liked to see one in action.<br>	So now I am on my way home and I am slowing down for a red light when I see the same Supra turbo with the high wing in a 7 Eleven shop.  So I rev it twice as I go by.  He pulls out and as soon as he does the light goes green and he floors it and flys by me.  So I catch up to him and notice that his tail lights are out so I tell him and he turns his lights on.  So I pull up along side at about 45 and we both punch it.  I am slowly starting to gain ground and then he shifts into the next gear and I hear the blowoff valve giving a mighty wail.  When he shifts is when I pull hard.  He did not miss <br>the shift either.  I pulled a quick 4-5 car lengths and seeing him deep in my <br>rearview I shut down and tap my brakes a couple of times to let him know that it is over and I won.  I was doing about 80 mph although I did not look at my speedo that is what I would guess as i had it floored for about 7 secs or so. So I slow down and wait for him to catch up and he slows down and pulls a u-turn and goes the other way so i try to give him a quick thumbs up but I <br>don't think he saw it.  Win no. 3.<br>	<br>Oh well another import killed along with a domestic.  For the night I was 3 for 3.  Feels pretty good. 
Z||000001||GREENDANO||06-19-99||06:11 AM||||Ah Ha!!!!<br>  So you're the reason the police look at me funny when I drive my Fiero by.  The were looking for a hot rodding Fiero that was blasting up and down the streets.   :)<br>  All I can say is BE CAREFUL!!!  Its a pretty big deal to get pulled over for street racing, let alone dangerous to everybody around you.  Have you every thought of racing it?  There has to be an SCCA event near-by.  Or even drag racing?  <br>  The guy that owned my GT before me used to drag race it just to blow of steam at a local track. I guess I'm old or don't want to abuse my equiptment, it doesn't interest me.<br>  I even own a big block Pro-street Ranger that has never been raced.<br>  Dan-O
